  "decision_conditions": [
    "The development to which this permission relates must be begun not later than the expiration of three years beginning with the date of the decision notice. \rReason: To comply with the provisions of S.51 of the Planning & Compulsory Purchase Act 2004. \r",
    "The development hereby permitted shall be carried out in accordance with the following approved plans:\r431A-A-EX.01\r431B-PA.06\r431B-PA.08\r431B-PA.09\r431B-PA.10\rHeritage Statement \rReason: For the avoidance of doubt and in the interests of proper planning\r",
    "The development shall not commence until details of the external finishing materials to be used have been submitted to and approved in writing by the Local Planning Authority. This should include a sample board of the proposed bricks to be used to match existing along with method of brick bonding and mortar jointing. The details should also provide written confirmation from a third-party supplier that a suitable quantity of bricks and coping stones to match the existing context of the building can be obtained. The development shall be constructed in accordance with the approved details. \r\rReason: To ensure a satisfactory external appearance and retain the character and appearance of the existing building and Southgate Circus Conservation Area.\r"
  ],
